Subject: Save the DMC sample byte, sweep reload and envelope restart flags in a state

A save-state fix, not an accuracy one: it changes nothing while a game runs.
FCEUSND_STATEINFO left out DMCDMABuf, the byte the DMC has fetched and not yet
shifted, sweepReload[] and each envelope's reloaddec, so a load kept whatever
the running game had in them. With nes_bench STATE=<n>, which saves a state,
loads it at the end of the run and plays the same frames again, Kirby's
Adventure (USA) (Rev 1) replayed the picture exactly but its sound differed
for 36 frames after a load at frame 300 and 26 after one at 1500, the samples
wrong from the eighth of the first frame on and the counts right, which is a
DMC level offset until the next $4011 write or sample. With these fields
saved every frame matches, as Castlevania and Zelda already did, the
benchmark's checksums are unchanged and AccuracyCoin is still 90 of 146.
States grow by 55 bytes; older states load, the missing chunks keeping the
running values as before.

License: GPL-2.0-or-later, as the FCEUmm code it changes (patches/fceumm/README.md).

---
diff --git a/src/sound.c b/src/sound.c
index 54c17dd..c931994 100644
--- a/src/sound.c
+++ b/src/sound.c
@@ -1431,6 +1431,16 @@ SFORMAT FCEUSND_STATEINFO[] = {
 	{ &sexyfilter2_acc, sizeof(sexyfilter2_acc) | FCEUSTATE_RLSB, "FAC3" },
 	{ &lq_tcout, sizeof(lq_tcout) | FCEUSTATE_RLSB, "TCOU"},
 
+	/* The DMC's fetched sample byte, the sweep units' reload flags and the
+	 * envelopes' restart flags are live state too: without them a load
+	 * plays a wrong DMC byte, which offsets the DMC level until the next
+	 * $4011 write or sample, and can skip a sweep or envelope restart. */
+	{ &DMCDMABuf, 1, "5DMB" },
+	{ sweepReload, 2, "SWRL" },
+	{ &EnvUnits[0].reloaddec, sizeof(EnvUnits[0].reloaddec) | FCEUSTATE_RLSB, "E0RD" },
+	{ &EnvUnits[1].reloaddec, sizeof(EnvUnits[1].reloaddec) | FCEUSTATE_RLSB, "E1RD" },
+	{ &EnvUnits[2].reloaddec, sizeof(EnvUnits[2].reloaddec) | FCEUSTATE_RLSB, "E2RD" },
+
 /* Historical note: this entry was excluded on big-endian hosts
  * (2018-12-14, Wii state-load failures). The root causes are gone:
  * FlipByteOrder's over-iteration no-op and ReadStateChunk's unchecked
